            "title": "docs: add medicus to community section",
            "body": "Adds `medicus` to the community list.\n\nMedicus is a health check library, not a hosted service. Its H3 handler (`medicus/h3`) runs custom checkers and responds with a JSON status. It works with H3 v1 and v2 and can be exported from a Nitro route file. MIT licensed, about 48k npm downloads a month.\n\n- npm: https://www.npmjs.com/package/medicus\n- repo: https://github.com/arthurfiorette/medicus\n- docs: https://medicus.js.org\n\nI'm the author.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added a community utility listing with details on its health checks, status responses, framework support, and repository link.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
