            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABPIpifw",
            "number": 1653,
            "title": "fix(response): run sync onResponse before returning the response",
            "body": "Resolves #1647\n\n## Summary\n\nInvoke `config.onResponse` synchronously inside `toResponse()` once `prepareResponse()` has produced a resolved `Response`, and only allocate the promise chain when `onResponse` returns a thenable. Dispose observation is extracted to a module-level `observeDispose()` helper so neither the no-hook path nor the sync-hook path allocates per-request closures.\n\n```diff\n toResponse(val, event, config)\n   prepareResponse(val, event, config) -> Response\n   if config.onResponse\n-    Promise.resolve()\n-      .then(() => onResponse(response, event))\n-      .catch(logError)\n-      .then(() => dispose?.observe(response, val) ?? response)\n+    try\n+      hookRes = onResponse(response, event)\n+      if typeof hookRes?.then === \"function\"\n+        return Promise.resolve(hookRes)\n+          .catch(logError)\n+          .then(() => observeDispose(event, response, val))\n+    catch (error)\n+      logError(error)\n+  return observeDispose(event, response, val)\n```\n\n- Reading `hookRes?.then` inside the `try` block ensures a custom object with a throwing `.then` getter is absorbed and logged the same way as a synchronous throw, while `Promise.resolve(hookRes)` adopts custom thenables whose `.then` throws on invocation or second read.\n- Adjusts bundle ceilings in `test/bench/bundle.test.ts` to match measured sizes (`H3Core`: `7952 B` / `3170 B gzip`, `defineHandler`: `7144 B` / `2903 B gzip`; `defineHandler` on `main` was already `7045 B` / `2872 B gzip` over the prior `7040` / `2870` budget).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** With a synchronous handler and synchronous `onResponse`, `app.fetch()` returned a `Promise<Response>` and queued three promise reactions per request; `onResponse` ran a microtask after `fetch()` returned.\n- **After:** `app.fetch()` returns a plain `Response` synchronously (`0` `PROMISE` allocations on warmup `fetch` loops), `onResponse` runs before `fetch()` returns, sync throws and throwing/rejecting thenables are absorbed without invoking `onError` or skipping `onDispose`, and `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm build`, and `pnpm vitest --run` pass (`75` files, `3355` passed).\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** Two-way\n\nIsolated to `toResponse()` in `src/response.ts` plus unit tests and bundle ceilings.\n\n**Blast Radius:** Narrow\n\n`toResponse()` and `app.fetch()` are already typed `Response | Promise<Response>` (and already returned a plain `Response` when `onResponse` was unset). Direct JS callers chaining `app.fetch(...).then(...)` without `await` or `Promise.resolve(...)` when both the handler and `onResponse` are synchronous now receive a `Response` directly, as noted in #1647.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Responses can now be returned synchronously when the response hook completes synchronously, avoiding unnecessary asynchronous behavior.\n  * When the response hook is asynchronous, the response waits for it to settle before cleanup runs.\n  * Errors from response hooks are logged unless silent mode is enabled, and do not trigger the request error handler.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
