        "t2": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABO88zIg",
            "number": 1652,
            "title": "fix(static): evaluate `If-Match` and `If-Unmodified-Since` preconditions",
            "body": "Resolves #1639.\n\n`serveStatic` now evaluates `If-Match` and `If-Unmodified-Since` before the existing `If-None-Match` / `If-Modified-Since` check, as RFC 9110 §13.2.2 orders them, and responds `412 Precondition Failed` when they fail:\n\n- `If-Match` uses strong comparison: `*` passes, a weak ETag never matches, and a missing ETag fails.\n- `If-Unmodified-Since` is only evaluated when `If-Match` is absent; an invalid date is ignored.\n\nThe check lives next to `isCacheMatch` in `src/utils/internal/cache.ts` as `isPreconditionFailed()`. Tests in `test/static.test.ts` (node and web) cover each case; they fail on main and pass with the change. `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` pass. In the full `pnpm vitest run`, only `test/bench/bundle.test.ts` (defineHandler bundle 7045 > 7040) fails, and it fails the same way on main locally.\n\nNot included: the `cache-control: no-store` header nitro adds on its 412, since h3 error responses don't carry headers set on `event.res`.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Static file requests now return a precondition failure when `If-Match` or `If-Unmodified-Since` conditions are not met, rather than returning a cached response. When both conditions are provided, `If-Match` takes precedence. Invalid date values are ignored.\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for ETag and date-based preconditions, including wildcard and list matching, condition precedence, supported date formats, and invalid dates.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
